{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nint main() {\n    ll n, m, mod;\n    scanf(\"%lld %lld %lld\", &n, &m, &mod);\n\n    vector<ll> fact(n + 1), inv(n + 1);\n    fact[0] = fact[1] = inv[0] = inv[1] = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i) {\n        ll r = mod / i;\n        ll x = mod - r * i;\n        fact[i] = fact[i - 1] * i % mod;\n        inv[i] = (mod - r * inv[x] % mod) % mod;\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i)\n        inv[i] = inv[i] * inv[i - 1] % mod;\n\n    ll total = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n        total = total * m % mod;\n\n    vector<int> bits(n + 1);\n    bits[0] = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i)\n        bits[i] = bits[i / 2] + (i % 2);\n\n    if (n & 1) {\n        printf(\"%lld\\n\", total);\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    int pop_n = bits[n];\n    vector<vector<ll>> dp(pop_n + 1, vector<ll>(n + 1, 0));\n    dp[0][0] = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < pop_n && i < m; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n; ++j) {\n            if (!dp[i][j]) continue;\n            int rem = n ^ j;\n            for (int s = rem; s > j; s = (s - 1) & rem) {\n                int state = s | j;\n                dp[i + 1][state] = (dp[i + 1][state] + dp[i][j] * inv[s] % mod) % mod;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 1; i <= m; ++i) {\n        ll term = dp[i][n];\n        term = term * fact[m] % mod;\n        term = term * inv[m - i] % mod;\n        term = term * fact[n] % mod;\n        total = (total - term % mod + mod) % mod;\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", total);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n        long m = sc.nextLong();\n        long mod = sc.nextLong();\n\n        long[] fact = new long[(int)n + 1];\n        long[] inv = new long[(int)n + 1];\n        fact[0] = fact[1] = inv[0] = inv[1] = 1;\n\n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i) {\n            long r = mod / i;\n            long x = mod - r * i;\n            fact[i] = fact[i - 1] * i % mod;\n            inv[i] = (mod - r * inv[(int)x] % mod) % mod;\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i)\n            inv[i] = inv[i] * inv[i - 1] % mod;\n\n        long total = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n            total = total * m % mod;\n\n        int[] bits = new int[(int)n + 1];\n        bits[0] = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i)\n            bits[i] = bits[i / 2] + (i % 2);\n\n        if ((n & 1) == 1) {\n            System.out.println(total);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        int pop_n = bits[(int)n];\n        long[][] dp = new long[pop_n + 1][(int)n + 1];\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < pop_n && i < m; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n; ++j) {\n                if (dp[i][j] == 0) continue;\n                int rem = (int)(n ^ j);\n                for (int s = rem; s > j; s = (s - 1) & rem) {\n                    int state = s | j;\n                    dp[i + 1][state] = (dp[i + 1][state] + dp[i][j] * inv[s] % mod) % mod;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (int i = 1; i <= m; ++i) {\n            long term = dp[i][(int)n];\n            term = term * fact[(int)m] % mod;\n            term = term * inv[(int)(m - i)] % mod;\n            term = term * fact[(int)n] % mod;\n            total = (total - term % mod + mod) % mod;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(total);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00011503035057103261, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0011486368020996451, -2.8967437174287625e-05, -0.012541121803224087, -0.4810636639595032, -7.390948667307384e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3007127310847864e-05, -0.000805053801741451, -7.271740287251305e-06, -0.012712983414530754, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.0001486429391661659, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -4.9828242481453344e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.00011419598013162613, -0.20244765281677246, -7.033323527139146e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1444026313256472e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.290122185717337e-05, -0.1128246933221817, -0.0003036991402041167, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -0.00018606838420964777, -8.129743218887597e-05, -4.768360213347478e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.9802276912960224e-06, 0.0, -0.007617474067956209, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -5.125986263010418e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00011944057769142091, -9.536738616588991e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.364403477869928e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -0.0019293281948193908, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.00029059001826681197, -4.6491513